function Stat({title,value,sub,icon}:{title:string;value:string;sub:string;icon:React.ReactNode}){return <article className="stat"><div>{title}<span>{icon}</span></div><strong>{value}</strong><small>{sub}</small></article>}
function PanelHead({title,sub,action}:{title:string;sub:string;action:()=>void}){return <div className="panelhead"><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{sub}</p></div><button className="icon" onClick={action}><ArrowUpRight size={16}/></button></div>}
function Field({name,label,placeholder,type='text',defaultValue}:{name:string;label:string;placeholder:string;type?:string;defaultValue?:string|number}){return <label className="field"><span>{label}</span><input name={name} type={type} placeholder={placeholder} defaultValue={defaultValue} required={name!=='due'&&name!=='progress'} min={type==='number'?0:undefined} max={name==='progress'?100:undefined}/></label>}
function Select({name,label,options,defaultValue}:{name:string;label:string;options:string[];defaultValue?:string}){return <label className="field"><span>{label}</span><select name={name} defaultValue={defaultValue??options[0]}>{options.map(o=><option key={o}>{o}</option>)}</select></label>}
function Automation(){const [enabled,setEnabled]=useState([true,true,false]);const rules=[['New lead follow-up','Create a follow-up task when a lead is added.','Lead created'],['Deadline nudge','Flag tasks due within the next 24 hours.','Daily check'],['Client approval reminder','Remind the project owner when feedback is pending.','Approval pending']];return <div className="autopage"><section className="hero smallhero"><div><div className="eyebrow lime"><Workflow size={14}/> SYSTEMS THAT WORK IN THE BACKGROUND</div><h2>Make repeatable work <em>automatic.</em></h2><p>Demo switches only change this local interface. Backend triggers come in a later milestone.</p></div></section><section className="panel">{rules.map((r,i)=><div className="autorow" key={r[0]}><div className="autoicon"><Workflow size={17}/></div><div><b>{r[0]}</b><p>{r[1]}</p><small>{r[2]}</small></div><button className={`toggle ${enabled[i]?'on':''}`} onClick={()=>setEnabled(a=>a.map((v,j)=>i===j?!v:v))}><i/></button></div>)}</section><p className="hint">Next: connect these rules to database events, scheduled jobs, and email notifications.</p></div>}


